    "seller_offer_identity_conflict_scope_v1": "The five frozen seller pages establish offer assertions rather than ten-week performance. Hershey SKU B01M68WYTJ is 6.87 dollars with no reviews shown; its title and quick look describe one 3.6-ounce pack of eight individually wrapped 45-percent-cocoa snack-size bars, while Product Dimensions reports 1.41 ounces. West End Foods SKU B075V1Y762 is 79.99 dollars with no reviews shown and its selected title and quick look describe five pounds of Ghirardelli 60-percent cacao squares, hand-picked and packed by West End Foods, without independently proving an original unit wrapper or ten-week outcome. Blue Diamond SKU B0051TPWG2 is 7.70 dollars, rated 83 percent over twelve reviews, and describes one 14-ounce resealable bag of almonds covered in cocoa powder and dark-chocolate flavor rather than a plain chocolate bar. Second Nature SKU B0758FJ52X is 39.85 dollars with no reviews shown and describes twelve 4.5-ounce resealable pouches of dark chocolate with almonds, cashews and pecans, plus a warm-weather shipping caution, while Product Dimensions reports only 4.5 ounces. Oh Nuts SKU B00C6ALV0U is 21.99 dollars, rated 85 percent over twelve reviews, and has a selected 2-pound offer with freshness and zip-lock claims while Package Dimensions reports 1.2 pounds. Exact delivered variants, net quantities, lots, dates, labels and package states remain unresolved.",
    "bloom_temper_crystal_boundary_v1": "Chocolate bloom is a whitish coating: fat bloom involves changes in fat crystals and sugar bloom involves moisture acting on sugar. The general source says bloom damages appearance and can make surface texture unappetizing without limiting shelf life, and describes bloomed chocolate as generally still edible. This classification does not prove cheap ingredients, authenticate an exact lot, or rule out contamination, allergens, package damage or a separate spoilage process. Tempering promotes glossy chocolate, snap, smooth texture and bloom resistance through controlled cocoa-butter crystallization, but the general mechanism does not verify the tempering history, crystal state or future result of any captured offer.",
    "oxidation_package_measurement_boundary_v1": "Autoxidation is oxygen-driven gradual degradation of organic compounds at ambient temperatures and can cause food rancidity through a free-radical chain process, but it supplies no exact nut-lot rate, induction time, package barrier or ten-week outcome. MVTR measures water-vapor passage and is strongly conditional on temperature, humidity gradient, thickness and method; sheet values do not establish whole-package performance because seams, creases, access points, heat seals and closures matter. OTR measures oxygen passage over time and likewise requires an exact material or complete-package test, with seals, joints and closures included. Generic mechanism pages cannot rank these five packages.",
    "community_operational_scope_v1": "The pocket-melt thread reports one foil-wrapped chocolate egg becoming gooey after several hours in a jeans pocket. The snack-bag thread recommends opening a bag, pushing air out and clipping it for travel, while a reply warns that opening replaces a nitrogen-rich headspace with oxygen and can accelerate staling. The labeling thread recommends marking decanted or stored containers to preserve identity and date information. The Boston thread asks where to buy block chocolate for bark and contains local, historical suggestions and preferences. These statements motivate heat-excursion logging, original-seal preservation, lot/date labeling and current local verification, but none is a controlled ten-week trial or evidence about the exact five offers.",
    "independent_unit_rotation_cost_v1": "Before committing to a rural stash, verify the exact SKU and selected variant, delivered unit count and net mass, current price and shipping, lot and best-before information, ingredients and allergens, manufacturer storage instructions, original wrapper or seal, package construction when available, and remedy terms. Preserve independent sealed units, label receipt and opening dates, and calculate waste-adjusted delivered cost per serving that remains acceptable at week ten. A large bag or five-pound bundle creates more exposure and waste risk than multiple independent units unless exact packaging and observed retention offset that commitment; sticker price, bulk mass, rating, resealability and seller freshness copy do not decide the comparison.",
    "staged_ten_week_sensory_protocol_v1": "Use the smallest reversible quantities and randomly allocate separate same-lot sealed units to weeks 0, 2, 6 and 10 when possible. Log pantry temperature, relative humidity and heat or moisture excursions; inspect identity, lot, date and seal before opening; photograph and separately classify bloom, package damage and other visible defects; smell before tasting and stop under predeclared safety or package-integrity rules. Record standardized aroma, snap or crispness, texture, stale or rancid notes, flavor and overall acceptability against a week-zero form-specific baseline. If matched current samples exist, code and randomize them for a paired or other discrimination test, but use separate acceptability scoring for preference and do not interpret a failure to detect difference as equality. Cross-product or cross-package causal claims require matched recipe, lot, storage and test conditions.",
    "stash_decision_preparation_v1": "Combine the literal offer audit, bloom and tempering boundary, autoxidation and package-measurement boundary, community operational variables, independent-unit rotation accounting and staged sensory protocol into one decision table. For each exact verified configuration, mark identity, package integrity, declared storage, week-ten acceptability and waste-adjusted delivered cost as pass, fail or unresolved. Do not let a pass on one axis compensate for a safety stop, package failure or unresolved exact identity, and do not rank products that were not tested under comparable declared conditions.",
    "evidence_bounded_stash_decision_v1": "The packet supports no immediate ten-week product winner. Treat bloom, tempering, autoxidation, MVTR, OTR and sensory discrimination as bounded mechanisms; retain seller quantity conflicts and forum scope; and verify every exact offer and package state. Begin with the smallest independent-unit commitment, run the declared week 0, 2, 6 and 10 protocol, and compare waste-adjusted delivered cost per accepted serving. Choose only the least-commitment exact configuration that passes identity, package, condition, week-ten sensory and waste-cost gates; if none passes or material fields remain unresolved, shorten the stocking horizon or defer. Do not infer a universal brand, format, barrier or safety winner."
